+```
+date<TAB>account<TAB>amount[<TAB>currency]
+```
+
+- `date`: ISO date (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
+- `amount`: up to two decimals, e.g. `-45.10`.
+- `currency` (optional): an ISO 4217 code of exactly three uppercase ASCII
+  letters, e.g. `EUR`. When the fourth column is absent the currency is `USD`.
+
+Blank lines and `#` comments are skipped.
+
+Output: `date,account,amount_cents,currency`, with the currency on every row.
+
+Exit status:
+
+- `0`: success.
+- `1`: any other input error (wrong field count, bad date, account or amount).
+- `2`: a malformed currency (not three uppercase ASCII letters).
+
+Errors go to stderr as `line N: ...`, where `N` is the input line number. The
+export stops at the first bad line.
